# build artifacts at the root and in any per-crate workspace (the wasm crate
# builds its own `crates/exav-unpack-wasm/target`)
target/
**/*.rs.bk
**/*.bak
Cargo.lock.orig
# downloaded signature DB and built caches (see `make cache`)
/exav-db/
*.cache
*.exavdb
# real-malware corpus must never be committed (the reproducible harness lives in
# scripts/, not here — corpus/ holds only local, gitignored samples + data)
/corpus/
*.malware
# real-malware test samples: kept locally (gitignored) for extra decoder
# coverage, NEVER committed — the tests that use them skip when absent, and CI
# relies on the synthetic/EICAR fixtures. Provenance (sha256) is in each dir's
# README.md. The synthetic `eicar.lnk` and the READMEs stay committed.
crates/exav-unpack/tests/fixtures/**/real-malware-*
/yara-x/
# internal strategy notes — never commit
/tmp/
/.claude/
# local secrets (API keys, e.g. MalwareBazaar Auth-Key) — never commit
.env.local
.env*.local
.env
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# …except the committed `.pyc` test fixtures, which are inputs to the scanner
# rather than build output of the scripts. Without this they are tracked while
# matching an ignore rule, so `git status` stays quiet about them but
# `git ls-files -ci` flags them, and the next person to trust the pattern
# deletes one.
!crates/exav-unpack/tests/fixtures/**/*.pyc
node_modules
test-results/
playwright-report/
# fuzz corpora and artifacts — never commit
fuzz/corpora/
.cargo/lld/
.cargo/config.toml
